{"event": "artifact", "agent": "documentation", "file": "README.md", "content": "# Inventory Manager\n\n## Purpose\nThe `Inventory` class provides a simple way to manage an inventory system where you can add products, increase or decrease their stock, and retrieve the current stock levels.\n\n## API\n\n### Class: `Inventory`\n\n#### Methods:\n1. **`add_product(name, quantity=0)`**\n   - Adds a new product to the inventory with the specified name and quantity.\n   - Raises `ValueError` if the product name is empty or if the initial quantity is negative.\n\n2. **`stock_in(name, quantity)`**\n   - Increases the stock of the specified product by the given quantity.\n   - Raises `ValueError` if the quantity is not a positive integer greater than 0.\n   - Raises `KeyError` if the product does not exist in the inventory.\n\n3. **`stock_out(name, quantity)`**\n   - Decreases the stock of the specified product by the given quantity.\n   - Raises `ValueError` if the quantity is not a positive integer greater than 0.\n   - Raises `KeyError` if the product does not exist in the inventory.\n   - Raises `ValueError` if the operation would result in a negative stock level.\n\n4. **`get_quantity(name)`**\n   - Returns the current stock quantity of the specified product.\n   - Raises `KeyError` if the product does not exist in the inventory.\n\n5. **`list_products()`**\n   - Returns a dictionary containing all products and their respective stock quantities.\n\n## Simple Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom inventory_manager import Inventory\n\ninventory = Inventory()\ninventory.add_product(\"Apples\", 10)\ninventory.stock_in(\"Apples\", 5)\ninventory.stock_out(\"Apples\", 3)\n\nprint(inventory.get_quantity(\"Apples\"))  # Output: 12\nprint(inventory.list_products())       # Output: {'Apples': 12}\n```\n\n## How to Run Pytest\n\nTo ensure your implementation meets the requirements, you can run the provided tests using `pytest`. Make sure you have `pytest` installed:\n\n```sh\npip install pytest\n```\n\nThen, run the tests:\n\n```sh\npytest test_inventory_manager.py\n```\n\nThis will execute the tests and provide feedback on whether your implementation is correct."}
{"event": "agent_end", "agent": "documentation", "step": 0}
